'''Wayland H. and Mamie Burt Stevens House''' is a historic home located at [[Fuquay-Varina, North Carolina|Fuquay-Varina]], [[Wake County, North Carolina]].  The house was built in 1936, and is a two-story, [[Colonial Revival architecture|Colonial Revival]]-style brick dwelling with a hipped roof. It features an entry [[portico]] and a front door with fanlight and sidelights. Also on the property are the contributing garage (1936) and tool shed (1936).<ref name = nrhpinv>{{Cite web | author = Sybil H. Argintar | title =Wayland H. and Mamie Burt Stevens House | work = National Register of Historic Places - Nomination and Inventory | date = July 2014 | url = https://files.nc.gov/ncdcr/nr/WA6549.pdf | format = pdf | publisher = North Carolina State Historic Preservation Office | accessdate = 2015-06-01}}</ref>

It was listed on the [[National Register of Historic Places]] in 2014.<ref name="nps"/>

