She completed [[kindergarten]] at Saint Vincent de Paul, attended [[primary school]] at Mama Mulezi, and earned her state [[diploma]] in [[biochemistry]] from Collège Mwanga de Goma.<ref name="RDC: À 20 ans, la jeune artiste Gloria Bash est l'artiste urbaine féminine la plus suivie sur YOUTUBE en RDC" /> After graduating in 2019, she enrolled at Université Catholique La Sapientia. In 2023, she graduated with distinction with a [[bachelor's degree]] in [[Legal science|legal]], [[Political science|political]], and administrative sciences.<ref name="RDC: À 20 ans, la jeune artiste Gloria Bash est l'artiste urbaine féminine la plus suivie sur YOUTUBE en RDC" />

=== 2022–2024: Rise on YouTube, ''Vodacom Best of the Best All Stars'', and releases ===
During an interview with Eventsrdc Radio in February 2022, Bash cited [[Fally Ipupa]] as her main musical inspiration and role model. She explained that she wanted audiences to discover her through his music because she admired his artistry and his approach to music.<ref name=":7" /> Encouraged by a close friend to pursue her musical talent, she created her first official [[YouTube channel]] in January 2022.<ref name="RDC: À 20 ans, la jeune artiste Gloria Bash est l'artiste urbaine féminine la plus suivie sur YOUTUBE en RDC" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Gloria... De chantre à artiste à succès |trans-title=Gloria... From singer to successful artist |url=https://gloriabash.com/biographie/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Gloria Bash |language=fr-FR}}</ref> Although concert halls and entertainment venues were shut down during the [[COVID-19 pandemic]], she continued performing online through [[Cover version|covers]], [[Medley (music)|medleys]] and [[Mashup (music)|mashups]] of songs by popular artists.<ref name=":0" /><ref name="RDC: À 20 ans, la jeune artiste Gloria Bash est l'artiste urbaine féminine la plus suivie sur YOUTUBE en RDC" /><ref name=":8">{{Cite web |last=Mpereng |first=Chadrack |date=11 January 2023 |title=Gloria Bash lance sa carrière avec le single "Koleya money" attendu ce vendredi |trans-title=Gloria Bash launches her career with the single "Koleya money" expected this Friday |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/gloria-bash-lance-sa-carriere-avec-le-single-koleya-money-attendu-ce-vendredi/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref name=":9">{{Cite web |last=Mpereng |first=Chadrack |date=15 January 2023 |title=Gloria Bash: Une grande première house pour "Koleya money" |trans-title=Gloria Bash: A major house premiere for "Koleya Money" |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/gloria-bash-une-grande-premiere-house-pour-koleya-money/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref> Her breakthrough came through a medley reinterpretation of Fally Ipupa's sixth studio album ''Tokooos II''.<ref name=":7" /><ref name=":10">{{Cite web |last=Kambala |first=Étienne |date=18 September 2022 |title=En huit mois, Gloria Bash dépasse le cap de 100.000 abonnés sur YouTube! |trans-title=In eight months, Gloria Bash surpassed 100,000 subscribers on YouTube! |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/en-huit-mois-gloria-bash-depasse-le-cap-de-100-000-abonnes-sur-youtube/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref name=":3" /> Bash told Eventsrdc Radio that she had always wanted to revisit ''Tokooos II'' in a different musical style because she had loved it since its release on 25 February 2022.<ref name=":7" /> With support and guidance from her manager, she used the project as a way to introduce herself to the public with something distinctive. Bash also briefed the press that she does not confine herself to one musical genre, as she feels comfortable adapting to different styles.<ref name=":7" /> The medley became popular in the Democratic Republic of the Congo and earned her the nickname "the female Fally Ipupa" from fans.<ref name=":3" />

In August 2022, she competed in Season 8 of ''Vodacom Best of the Best All Stars'', the Congolese adaptation of the international [[Reality television|reality TV]] franchise ''[[Idol (franchise)|Idol]]'', which was organized by [[Vodacom#Member companies|Vodacom Congo]] and Pygma Communication. The competition offered a [[Dollar sign|$]]20,000 prize along with a recording contract with [[Sony Music Africa]].<ref name=":11">{{Cite web |last=Lutete |first=Michée |date=12 August 2022 |title=Vodacom Best of the Best prime 3: la mauvaise note de Gloria Bash |trans-title=Vodacom Best of the Best Prime 3: Gloria Bash's poor rating |url=https://www.lemag.cd/evenement/2022/08/12/vodacom-best-best-prime-3-la-mauvaise-note-de-gloria-bash |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Lemag |language=fr}}</ref><ref name=":4" /> She represented [[North Kivu]] and performed the 2003 [[zouk]] song "Mon Soleil" by [[Martinique|Martinican]] singer Princess' Lover during the third round, but her performance "failed to impress the jury" and she did not qualify for the final after receiving scores of 4/10, 4/10, and 3/10.<ref name=":11" /><ref name=":3" /> Jury member [[Koffi Olomide|Koffi Olomidé]] stated that she was not the contestant he would have chosen to represent the country, particularly because the round's theme was "You must convey emotion".<ref name=":11" />

By September 2022, Bash's [[YouTube]] covers were rapidly gaining attention. Her most viewed video was an [[Amapiano]]-style cover of [[Buga (song)|Buga]] by [[Kizz Daniel]] and [[Tekno (musician)|Tekno]], which reached 2.2 million views in three months. This was followed by her cover medley of ''Tokooos II'' with 695,000 views in six months, while her video "Le mélange de la musique ivoirienne et congolaise" ranked third with 433,000 views in five months.<ref name=":10" /> On 13 January 2023, she released the Amapiano-inspired single "Koleya Money" through Playone France.<ref name=":8" /><ref name=":9" /> She later released "Alakini" on 20 June, a song centered on hope, solidarity, and unity amid the [[M23 campaign (2022–present)|ongoing M23 conflict]] in eastern Congo.<ref name=":3" /> The same theme continued with "To Kufi", released on 15 February 2024. On 14 May 2024, Bash collaborated with rapper Yvon Yusuf on "Mbele". The [[Congo Swahili|Swahili]] title means "ahead" or "forward", and the song encourages perseverance and ignoring criticism.<ref name=":12">{{Cite web |last=Mandina |first=Hervé |date=30 May 2024 |title=Afro-Club, le Hit des platines avec Wayé et Lema, Minz et Davido, Gloria Bash et Yvan Yusuf |trans-title=Afro-Club, the hit on the turntables with Wayé and Lema, Minz and Davido, Gloria Bash and Yvan Yusuf |url=https://www.rfi.fr/fr/musique/20240530-afro-club-le-hit-des-platines-avec-way%C3%A9-et-lema-minz-et-davido-gloria-bash-et-yvan-yusuf |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Rfi.fr/fr/musique |publisher=[[Radio France Internationale]] |language=fr |publication-place=Paris, France}}</ref><ref name=":13">{{Cite web |last=Mandina |first=Hervé |date=19 December 2024 |title=Afro-Club, le Hit des platines avec Dorty, Bobo Wê et Big MJ |trans-title=Afro-Club, the hit on the turntables with Dorty, Bobo Wê and Big MJ |url=https://www.rfi.fr/fr/musique/20241219-afro-club-le-hit-des-platines-avec-dorty-bobo-w%C3%AA-et-big-mj |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Rfi.fr/fr/musique |publisher=[[Radio France Internationale]] |language=fr |publication-place=Paris, France}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mpereng |first=Chadrack |date=27 May 2024 |title="Mbele", Gloria Bash inaugure son premier duo de carrière avec Yvon Yusuf |trans-title="Mbele", Gloria Bash inaugurates her first career duet with Yvon Yusuf |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/mbele-gloria-bash-inaugure-son-premier-duo-de-carriere-avec-yvon-yusuf/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref> She later appeared on "Épuisée" by [[Butembo]]-born rapper Alia Kas on 26 June, although the [[music video]] had premiered earlier on 15 June.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Johnson |first=Verite |date=18 June 2024 |title=Alia Kas et Gloria Bash: un feat entre deux pépites "épuisées" |trans-title=Alia Kas and Gloria Bash: A collab between two "exhausted" gems |url=https://buniaactualite.cd/alia-kas-et-gloria-bash-un-feat-entre-deux-pepites-epuisees/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Bunia Actualité |language=fr-FR}}</ref> On 24 August 2024, Bash released the [[Afrobeats]]-inspired single "Cascade" under Black Star France, the label founded by [[Cameroon]]ian businessman and producer Walter Tchassem, rapper [[Timati]] and Congolese-French singer and rapper [[Gims]] to promote young French and African talent internationally.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kabamba |first=Jérémie |date=2 September 2024 |title=Gloria Bash vous présente son nouveau clip "Cascade" (VIDÉO) |trans-title=Gloria Bash presents her new music video "Cascade" (VIDEO) |url=https://www.strong2kinmoov.com/2024/09/02/gloria-bash-vous-presente-son-nouveau-clip-cascade-video/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Strong2kin Moov |language=fr-FR |publication-place=Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of the Congo}}</ref><ref name=":14">{{Cite web |last=Mpereng |first=Chadrack |date=7 December 2024 |title=Signée chez Black Star France, Gloria Bash franchit un nouveau cap dans sa carrière |trans-title=Signed to Black Star France, Gloria Bash takes a new step in her career |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/signee-chez-black-star-france-gloria-bash-franchit-un-nouveau-cap-dans-sa-carriere/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref name=":13" /> In December 2024, she officially signed with the label after Gims reportedly discovered her talent during a visit to [[Goma]].<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |date=9 December 2024 |title=RD Congo: Gloria Bash rejoint le Label Black Star France de Gims |url=https://www.musicinafrica.net/fr/magazine/rd-congo-gloria-bash-rejoint-le-label-black-star-france-de-gims |access-date=31 December 2024 |website=Music In Africa |language=fr|trans-title=DR Congo: Gloria Bash joins Gims' Black Star France label|last=Matanda|first=Alvin}}</ref><ref name=":14" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mande |first=Ordi |date=7 December 2024 |title=Gims signe Gloria Bash chez Black Star France |trans-title=Gims signs Gloria Bash to Black Star France |url=https://mbote.cd/a-la-une/gims-signe-gloria-bash-chez-black-star-france/172754/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Mbote |language=fr-FR |publication-place=Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of the Congo}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mugisho |first=Bashomba |title=Gloria Bash voit grand avec Black Star France |url=https://ouragan.cd/2024/12/gloria-bash-voit-grand-avec-black-star-france |access-date=31 December 2024 |website=Ouragan.cd |language=FR|date=8 December 2024|trans-title=Gloria Bash has big plans with Black Star France}}</ref> That same month, she released the single "Toza Bien".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Masamba |first=Plamedi |date=14 December 2024 |title=Gloria Bash lance l'aventure chez Black Star France avec "Toza Bien" (VIDÉOCLIP) |trans-title=Gloria Bash launches her adventure with Black Star France with "Toza Bien" (MUSIC VIDEO) |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/gloria-bash-lance-laventure-chez-black-star-france-avec-toza-bien-videoclip/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref><ref name=":13" />

=== 2025–present: ''Solidarité Congo'' concert, standalone releases, ''Patrona'', and ''Zoshi'' ===
On 7 March 2025, Bash released "Ada".<ref name=":15">{{Cite web |last=Mandina |first=Hervé |date=7 August 2025 |title=Afro-Club et Afro-Club Deluxe - Gloria Bash revient avec "Fond de teint", une ode à l'authenticité |trans-title=Gloria Bash returns with "Fond de teint", an ode to authenticity |url=https://www.rfi.fr/fr/podcasts/afro-club-le-hit-des-platines/20250807-gloria-bash-revient-avec-fond-de-teint-une-ode-%C3%A0-l-authenticit%C3%A9 |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Rfi.fr/fr/podcasts |publisher=[[Radio France Internationale]] |language=fr |publication-place=Paris, France}}</ref> The next month, on 22 April, during the ''Solidarité Congo'' [[benefit concert]] at [[Accor Arena]] attended by more than 22,000 spectators, [[Gims]] surprised the crowd by inviting her onstage during his closing performance. After performances by artists such as [[Youssoupha]], [[Singuila]], [[Gazo (rapper)|Gazo]], [[Dadju]], and [[Fally Ipupa]], she performed several of her own songs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Masamba |first=Plamedi |date=25 April 2025 |title=Concert Solidarité Congo: "Voilà le public français", le coup de projecteur monumental de Gims sur Gloria Bash |trans-title=Congo Solidarity Concert: "This is the French public," Gims' monumental spotlight on Gloria Bash |url=https://www.eventsrdc.com/concert-solidarite-congo-voila-le-public-francais-le-coup-de-projecteur-monumental-de-gims-sur-gloria-bash/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Eventsrdc.com |language=fr-FR}}</ref> On 4 July, Bash issued the single "Fond de teint", which was described by [[Radio France Internationale]] as "a true declaration of [[self-love]]" that encourages young women to value themselves beyond [[Human physical appearance|physical appearances]].<ref name=":15" /> She later released "Mabega" on 12 September.<ref name=":16">{{Cite web |title=Toutes les chansons de Gloria Bash - Discographie |trans-title=All songs by Gloria Bash – Discography |url=https://gloriabash.com/musique/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Gloria Bash |language=fr-FR}}</ref>

Her debut [[Extended play|Extended Play]] (EP), ''Patrona'', was issued on 1 November 2025 and featured nine songs plus a [[bonus track]]. It was by singles "Koleya money", "Hau Shalange", "Love Taste", and "Die Die".<ref name=":12" /> On 7 November, she followed with the [[zouk]]-inspired love song "Amour Amour", which is noted for its "perfect symphony of meticulously combined instruments".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kombi |first=Gaéthan |date=12 November 2025 |title="Amour Amour": Gloria Bash se noie dans un verre de mélancolie |trans-title="Love Love": Gloria Bash drowns in a glass of melancholy |url=https://totalementactus.net/amour-amour-gloria-bash-se-noie-dans-un-verre-de-melancolie/ |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Totalement Actus |language=fr-FR}}</ref> She later released "Toleka" on 19 December and "Milele" on 6 March 2026.<ref name=":16" />

On 10 May 2026, Bash released her second seven-track EP, ''Zoshi'', which features two bonus tracks and a guest appearance by The Mingongo.<ref name=":5" /><ref name=":6" />

== Controversies ==
=== AI-generated image ===
On 25 November 2025, a photo showing a young woman in a [[bikini]] on a beach began circulating on the [[Facebook page]] Kivu Masolo, which had more than 2,600 [[Friending and following|followers]]. The post described the image as a "sexy revelation for the first time" and alleged that the woman was Bash.<ref name=":17">{{Cite web |last=Kasoki |first=Isabelle |date=6 December 2025 |title=Faux, cette prétendue photo de Gloria Bash en bikini est une image générée par intelligence artificielle |trans-title=False, this supposed photo of Gloria Bash in a bikini is an image generated by artificial intelligence |url=https://elezafact.cd/article/soci%C3%A9t%C3%A9/faux-cette-pretendue-photo-de-gloria-bash-en-bikini-est-une-image-generee-par-intelligence-artificielle |access-date=10 May 2026 |website=Elezafact.cd |publisher=Eleza Fact |language=fr |publication-place=Goma, North Kivu, Democratic Republic of the Congo}}</ref> According to the accompanying rumor, the picture had supposedly been taken in [[Kinshasa]] during celebrations surrounding her song "Mabega", which premiered on 12 September 2025. The image was widely shared across social media, and it soon fueled confusion and spread misinformation among internet users. As commonly happens with [[Sensationalism|sensational online]] content, the image circulated rapidly without verification.<ref name=":17" />

Bash denied being the woman shown in the image, stating: "...You can clearly see that it's an image created with [[Artificial intelligence|AI]]". Eleza Fact, a [[fact-checking]] organization based in [[Goma]], launched an investigation that combined Bash's direct testimony with technical examinations using [[Artificial intelligence content detection|AI-detection]] tools. Hive Moderation, a professional platform specializing in identifying [[AI art|AI-generated visuals]], assigned the image a 98.4% probability of being artificially generated.<ref name=":17" /> A second analysis conducted with Fake Image Detector, another tool designed to identify manipulated or [[Computer-generated imagery|computer-generated visuals]], also confirmed that the picture had been digitally created or altered. Isabelle Kasoki of Eleza Fact stated that the incident represented a form of gender-based digital violence in which artificially suggestive images are used to sexualize and humiliate women.<ref name=":17" /> As part of the [[16 Days of Activism against Gender-based Violence|16 Days of Activism]] campaign, the organization stressed that sharing intimate or allegedly intimate content without consent — even when created through artificial intelligence — amounts to violence intended to undermine women's dignity, reputation, and [[Insecurity (emotion)|emotional security]]. Kasoki added that such practices can encourage [[blackmail]], [[Social stigma|stigmatization]], and [[Peer pressure|societal pressure]], especially toward women who hold public visibility or political influence.<ref name=":17" />

